Documentation to navigate the quest::

Part 1 ::
============
Step 1: Republish the dataset to S3
The source URL is a directory listing (https://download.bls.gov/pub/time.series/pr/), which contains multiple text files.
You’ll need to:
Scrape the file list (since it’s an Apache-style directory index).
Download each file locally (or stream).
Upload to your S3 bucket.

Step 2: Keep S3 in Sync with Source
The requirements mean:
Detect new files → If new files are added to the BLS site, copy them to S3.
Detect deleted files → If a file disappears from the site, remove it from S3.
Avoid duplicates → Don’t re-upload files if they haven’t changed.

The typical way is:
Maintain a manifest of checksums (MD5/SHA) or compare LastModified headers.
Compare source file list vs S3 file list.

