==============
Step 1: Didnot create data pipelines due to no accessibility to the AWS environment. 
Step 2: Create a folder lambda_src/ with two files: ingest_lambda.py and report_lambda.py.
#ingest_lambda.py
This lambda:
-Scrapes https://download.bls.gov/pub/time.series/pr/ for file links (no BeautifulSoup — uses a regex).
-Downloads each file, calculates MD5, compares to S3 ETag (if present) to avoid re-uploading.
-Deletes S3 objects that are no longer present on the source site (keeps bucket in sync).
-Calls the DataUSA API and writes the JSON to S3 under the datausa-population/ prefix with timestamp.
 #report_lambda.py
This lambda:
-Is triggered by SQS messages containing S3 event notifications (S3 -> SQS).
-For each S3 created JSON (the DataUSA file), reads it from S3 and also reads pr.data.0.Current CSV from S3.
-Uses pandas to compute:
--Mean and stddev of US population for years 2013–2018.
--For each series_id, the year with maximum sum of value (sum of quarters).
--For PRS30006032 and Q01, produces a joined row with population for that year.
-Logs results to CloudWatch.                                      
